a score, and Western Michigan defeated Akron 42-14 on Tuesday night.","story":"AKRON, Ohio -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5085006/jalen-buckley\" target=\"_new\">Jalen Buckley</a> dashed for 121 yards and two touchdowns, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4917858/cole-cabana\" target=\"_new\">Cole Cabana</a> added 107 rushing yards and a score, and Western Michigan defeated Akron 42-14 on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              The Broncos (7-3, 5-1 Mid-American Conference) opened their mid-week MACtion slate in convincing fashion, out-gaining Akron 566-233 and holding possession for nearly 43 minutes of clock.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5074245/broc-lowry\" target=\"_new\">Broc Lowry</a> completed all 15 of his passing attempts for 149 yards and a score, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5145473/mason-reynolds\" target=\"_new\">Mason Reynolds</a> was 7-for-8 passing for 57 yards and two touchdowns.\n\n\r\n              Western Michigan scored on three straight drives in the first half, as <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5157528/nate-levicki\" target=\"_new\">Nate Levicki</a> caught a 3-yard score and Cole Cabana broke free for an 82-yard dash to the end zone to complete a 98-yard drive. Buckley punched it in from the 1-yard line to send WMU into halftime up 21-7.\n\n\r\n              Buckley added his second on a 35-yard rush in the third, Keivin Boone-Nelson caught a 20-yarder, and Levicki caught his second score for 10 yards to round out the scoring.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5198324/cibastian-broughton\" target=\"_new\">Cibastian Broughton</a> threw for 173 yards and two touchdowns for the Zips (1-9, 0-6).\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Western Michigan: host Eastern Michigan next Tuesday with a chance to win their third Michigan MAC Trophy in the past four years.\n\n\r\n              Akron: at UMass next Wednesday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>, visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-basketball-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/mens-college-basketball\">men’s basketball coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-11T03:23:34Z"}}